specs/hal-engine-npm-release/tasks.md:29:- [x] T006 **Blocker.** Record the repository-visibility decision in `adrs/`: publishing with `--provenance` requires a publicly resolvable source repository, so the release workflow either carries the flag or it does not. State the rule generally enough that a later package reads it rather than re-deriving it, and frame the trade honestly — the built package is public either way, so visibility decides the history, the tests, the examples and the issue record, and exposure covers every commit rather than the tip. T011 cannot be finished until this lands.
specs/hal-engine-npm-release/tasks.md:31:- [x] T008 [P] Audit the build chain from a job that fails. Add `scripts/check-audit.mjs` (full installed tree, no `--omit=dev`, fails at `high` and above, reads committed acceptances carrying advisory/package/reason/ISO expiry/acknowledged-by, an expired entry fails too) and `scripts/check-action-pins.mjs` (every `uses:` is a 40-hex SHA — the three workflows present today are not). Add a `check:build-chain` script and a CI job. Keep `supertest` — `src/transport/routes/chats.test.ts` imports it, so an earlier zero-occurrence measurement no longer holds. Baseline before the work: 18 advisories, 1 critical / 6 high; `npm audit fix` takes it to 3, none at high or above, lockfile only.
specs/hal-engine-npm-release/tasks.md:34:- [x] T011 Publish from a `v*` tag. Add `.github/workflows/publish.yml` (Trusted Publishing over OIDC, no `NPM_TOKEN`, `--access public`, `--provenance` per T006's answer) and `scripts/check-version.sh` (tag vs. committed version, a script so it runs before a tag is pushed). Call the T008 and T009 checks before `npm publish`, add a step that fails when the pack list contains any `*.test.*` entry, and a step that fails when the tagged commit is not an ancestor of `origin/main` - a tag can be pushed from any branch, and publishing over OIDC is what makes push access to `main` the right to release. Add § Releasing to `AGENTS.md`: bump in the PR, merge, tag `vX.Y.Z` on `main`, push. `npm ci --ignore-scripts` throughout, because `prepare` runs on both `ci` and `publish`. Depends on T009, T010, T006.
specs/hal-engine-npm-release/tasks.md:36:- [x] T032 [P] Alarm on a commit that reaches `main` outside a pull request. Add `.github/workflows/guard-main-pushes.yml` — `on: push: branches: [main]`, least privilege (`contents: read`, `issues: write`, `pull-requests: read`), and a job that resolves each pushed commit to its associated pull requests and opens one issue per commit that has none, naming the sha, the author and the committer. Branch protection is the lock and this is the detector behind it: `main` requires a PR, blocks force-pushes and deletion, and enforces all of it for admins, but a protection rule that is relaxed or bypassed leaves no alarm of its own. It matters in this repository specifically because T011 authenticates to the registry over OIDC with nothing stored to revoke, so push access to `main` is transitively the right to publish under the scope. Must land before T031; depends on nothing.
specs/hal-engine-npm-release/tasks.md:40:Independent of phase 2 and runnable alongside it. All of it must land before
specs/hal-engine-npm-release/tasks.md:67:- [x] T026 [P] Mark the two spikes. **Three, not two**: `docs/spikes/mcp.md` is also unmarked, and T025 has just added a fourth file to the directory with a block whose shape the others should match. A status blockquote after the H1 and before the first `##` in `docs/spikes/spike-ai-response-validation.md` and `docs/spikes/spike-bedrock-integration.md`, stating what shipped, what is superseded and what is still open. Nothing below the block changes. They were moved during the spec restructure but never marked, and they still rank top for an observability question. Done for all three; each diff is insertion-only, and each block cites the ADR that says whether the design shipped.
